{"message":"For minimizing ATM costs abroad, the Bluest Account appears to be the best option among the accounts reviewed: it charges $0 in Rho-Bank foreign ATM withdrawal fees and rebates third-party ATM operator fees up to $50 per monthly statement cycle. Over a three-month trip, that could cover up to $150 in operator fees, subject to the monthly limits. The ATM operator may still charge a fee initially, and rebates are limited to $50 per cycle.

World Blue also has a $0 Rho foreign ATM fee and rebates up to $100 per calendar month, but it carries a $50 monthly maintenance fee, requires maintaining at least $10,000, and appears designed for international business checking. Other reviewed accounts charge percentage-based foreign ATM fees.

I don’t have a confirmed Bluest monthly maintenance fee or personal-account eligibility requirements in the available information, so I can’t calculate your total cost conclusively. If you’d like, I can help you proceed with the Bluest Account after confirming your account type and verifying your identity."}
